  "Id": 1686,
  "Title": "Shoulder Dystocia Team Training Workshops",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Two Team Training Workshops on Shoulder Dystocia were organised at CIME. ",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Shoulder dystocia is an acute, usually unanticipated, obstetric\nemergency, complicating about 1% of vaginal deliveries. Essentially the baby's\nhead is born but his or her shoulders get stuck in the birth canal. When this\nhappens and isn't responded to immediately, then the baby's life is at risk or\ncan suffer permanent brachial plexus injury, or brain damage. These situations\nrequire prompt diagnosis and action, mobilizing obstetricians, midwives and\npaediatricians to prevent serious consequences to mother and baby."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The first workshop was attended by Medical Officers and Midwives from\nfour AKU secondary care centres (Garden, Kharadar, Karimabad and Hyderabad).\nThe second workshop was organised in collaboration with Getz Pharma for\ncandidates outside AKU. The candidates were from Liaquat National Hospital,\nCivil Hospital Karachi, Sindh Government Hospital Saudabad and other local\nmaternity homes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The sessions included a short introductory lecture on Shoulder dystocia,\nfollowed by training on the performance of manoeuvres on the PROMPT model. The\ncandidates were briefed about the simulation and then immersed in a simulation\nscenario where they had to work as a team to resolve shoulder dystocia on our\nnew high-fidelity simulator 'Victoria'. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
